==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*fedwōr}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*kʷetwóres}}.

Common Germanic cognates include Old High German [[fior]] (German ''[[vier]]''), Old Saxon [[fiuwar]], Old Dutch [[viuwar]] (Dutch ''[[vier]]''), Old Norse ''[[fjórir]]'', Gothic {{l|got|𐍆𐌹𐌳𐍅𐍉𐍂}}.

Indo-European cognates include Proto-Slavic {{term/t|sla-pro|*četyre}} (Russian {{l|ru|четыре}}), Old Irish [[cethair]], Greek {{term|τέσσαρες|lang=grc}}, Latin ''[[quattuor]]''.

